00:35:48.760 --> 00:35:50.716
- He's got a moral compass.
- That's right.


00:35:51.000 --> 00:35:53.434
Moral compass? I'm an entertainer,
not Christopher bleeding Columbus.


00:35:53.560 --> 00:35:55.118
Oi, what do you think of that?


00:35:55.240 --> 00:35:57.356
Nah, that's too, uh, too romantic.
Here you go.


00:35:57.480 --> 00:35:58.799
Is that all?


00:35:58.920 --> 00:36:00.592
- It's been a slow week.
- Ian?


00:36:01.560 --> 00:36:02.879
Uh, too satanic.


00:36:03.480 --> 00:36:05.391
Oi, oi, what's wrong with that one?


00:36:05.800 --> 00:36:07.836
- You're always giving me that one.
- Yeah, and?


00:36:08.120 --> 00:36:09.678
We know all about that, Ian.


00:36:09.960 --> 00:36:12.349
Oh, no, no, Chaz, Chaz, Chaz. That,


00:36:12.560 --> 00:36:15.358
that is a riddle. It's a love song.
It's a questioning.


00:36:15.600 --> 00:36:17.318
It's a striving of the human soul.


00:36:17.600 --> 00:36:19.989
It's just...
It's called <i>Sex, Drugs & Rock & Roll.</i>


00:36:20.720 --> 00:36:21.755
That's good.


00:36:21.880 --> 00:36:23.598
- Mmm-mmm, it's too obvious.
- Tell him, Denny.


00:36:23.800 --> 00:36:25.199
Look, it's a celebration. It's...


00:36:25.320 --> 00:36:28.039
It's an anthem for all the outsiders,
for all the uglies,


00:36:28.160 --> 00:36:29.434
for all the freaks, you know,


00:36:29.560 --> 00:36:33.348
who are slaving away every day
in their shit shirts


00:36:33.480 --> 00:36:36.631
and their shit shoes,
trying to fit in.


00:36:36.760 --> 00:36:38.716
"Is that all there is to life?"
They ask.


00:36:39.440 --> 00:36:41.829
And then, lo and behold...


00:36:46.360 --> 00:36:49.397
- Can you dance to that, Denny?
- Yeah, if you dance with me.


00:36:49.560 --> 00:36:51.039
You nicked that.


00:36:51.160 --> 00:36:52.957
God, everyone's a critic these days,
aren't they?


00:36:54.080 --> 00:36:57.470
The immature artist plagiarises
and the mature artist steals.


00:36:57.960 --> 00:36:59.473
And I am about to grow up.


00:37:05.920 --> 00:37:07.876
Sex, drugs and rock and roll.


00:37:09.600 --> 00:37:10.919
Okay, how about...


00:37:12.600 --> 00:37:14.795
See? Blue's your colour,
you know that?


00:37:15.480 --> 00:37:16.913
That's it. That's it.


00:37:18.720 --> 00:37:21.188
<i>#</i> Grey is such a pity


00:37:22.360 --> 00:37:24.351
Yeah! Look at you all! Look, look.


00:37:24.520 --> 00:37:27.478
- You're magnificent!
- You are gonna be


00:37:27.720 --> 00:37:29.392
- just like your dad.
- No, no.


00:37:29.560 --> 00:37:30.879
- A proper little geezer.
- No.


00:37:31.000 --> 00:37:32.319
- Baxter, come on.
- Don't.


00:37:32.440 --> 00:37:33.714
Baxter, stop fidgeting.


00:37:33.840 --> 00:37:35.193
- Bax...
- Stop it.


00:37:35.320 --> 00:37:36.639
- Don't be such a baby.
- Get off.


00:37:40.360 --> 00:37:41.759
Who did that?


00:37:41.880 --> 00:37:45.190
Boys. Bigger boys.


00:37:47.280 --> 00:37:49.157
They said I was posh.


00:37:50.320 --> 00:37:51.673
Are we posh?


00:37:53.080 --> 00:37:55.071
No, we're arts and crafts.


00:37:56.320 --> 00:37:58.151
That's what we are.
We're arts and crafts.


00:38:04.400 --> 00:38:06.038
There. That's handsome, isn't it?


00:38:28.480 --> 00:38:29.754
Baxter!


00:38:30.440 --> 00:38:31.919
There he is, here's my son.


00:38:32.160 --> 00:38:34.037
These are all my friends.
Say hi to Baxter, everybody.


00:38:34.160 --> 00:38:36.037
Big round of applause for my son.


00:38:36.640 --> 00:38:38.517
Baxter Front, I like to call him.


00:38:42.760 --> 00:38:44.159
Listen, we haven't tried
this one before.


00:38:44.280 --> 00:38:46.157
It's a little experimentation.
Oi, Chaz, let's start this up.


00:38:46.280 --> 00:38:48.669
We'll go for the rock. We'll have
white face, black shirt, white socks.


00:38:48.800 --> 00:38:50.153
One, two, three, four.


00:38:50.880 --> 00:38:52.711
<i>#</i> Who, who, who slapped John?


00:38:55.800 --> 00:38:57.074
<i>#</i> White face, black shirt


00:38:57.200 --> 00:38:58.474
<i>#</i> White socks, black shoes


00:38:58.600 --> 00:39:00.875
<i>#</i> Black hair, white Strat,
bled white, died black


00:39:01.320 --> 00:39:03.550
<i>#</i> Sweet Gene Vincent


00:39:04.000 --> 00:39:06.230
<i>#</i> There's one in every town


00:39:06.840 --> 00:39:08.592
<i>#</i> And the devil drives


00:39:08.720 --> 00:39:10.039
<i>#</i> Till the hearse arrives


00:39:10.160 --> 00:39:11.912
<i>#</i> And you lay that pistol down


00:39:12.040 --> 00:39:13.268
Just keep singing that last verse.


00:39:13.400 --> 00:39:15.072
<i>#</i> Sweet Gene Vincent


00:39:15.760 --> 00:39:17.876
<i>#</i> There's one in every town


00:39:18.560 --> 00:39:20.437
<i>#</i> And the devil drives
till the hearse...


00:39:20.800 --> 00:39:22.358
Keep singing!


00:39:24.320 --> 00:39:26.550
<i>#</i> Sweet Gene Vincent


00:39:35.440 --> 00:39:36.759
I hope you don't mind me saying,


00:39:36.920 --> 00:39:38.239
but you are being a bit
of a right old moody.


00:39:38.520 --> 00:39:39.919
We said we'd look after him, Ian.


00:39:40.160 --> 00:39:41.718
Yeah, I know. He's my son.


00:39:41.840 --> 00:39:43.671
- I've got him a driver and everything.
- What, someone reliable?


00:39:44.200 --> 00:39:45.952
Yeah, yeah, of course.


00:39:46.080 --> 00:39:47.274
- Really?
- I mean, the man was


00:39:47.400 --> 00:39:48.958
a roadie with Led Zeppelin,
for fuck's sake.


00:39:49.080 --> 00:39:50.911
All right, Baxter?


00:39:51.400 --> 00:39:53.038
I've got a little surprise for you.


00:39:53.720 --> 00:39:56.632
Ooh, speak of the devil,
and he will appear.


00:39:57.120 --> 00:39:59.634
Can you feel him slouching
ever nearer?


00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:03.913
Ooh, has Santa Claus come
early this year? No...


00:40:04.040 --> 00:40:06.713
It's the Sulphate Strangler!


00:40:18.720 --> 00:40:22.235
<i>#</i> The sons of the prophet
were brave men and bold


00:40:22.440 --> 00:40:24.431
<i>#</i> And quite unaccustomed to fear


00:40:24.760 --> 00:40:27.672
<i>#</i> But the bravest by far
in the ranks of the Shah


00:40:27.960 --> 00:40:30.758
<i>#</i> Was Abdulla Bulbul Ameer


00:40:31.120 --> 00:40:33.429
<i>#</i> One day, this bold Russian


00:40:33.880 --> 00:40:35.393
<i>#</i> He shouldered his gun


00:40:36.000 --> 00:40:38.560
<i>#</i> And donned his most truculent sneer


00:40:38.680 --> 00:40:41.752
<i>#</i> Downtown he did go,
where he trod on the toe


00:40:42.160 --> 00:40:45.038
<i>#</i> Of Abdulla Bulbul Ameer


00:40:48.560 --> 00:40:51.120
- Watch it!
- Oh, shit! Oh, sorry.


00:40:53.720 --> 00:40:55.119
Lovely.


00:41:56.600 --> 00:41:58.033
You all right, Dad?


00:42:17.160 --> 00:42:18.991
<i>I'm doing pretty good</i>
<i>at the moment, you know.</i>


00:42:20.440 --> 00:42:21.998
<i>You should come and see me.</i>


00:42:22.800 --> 00:42:24.358
<i>Would you like that?</i>


00:43:35.480 --> 00:43:38.313
<i>#</i> The sons of the
prophet were brave men and bold


00:43:38.440 --> 00:43:40.237
<i>#</i> And quite unaccustomed to fear


00:43:44.240 --> 00:43:48.518
Your mum told your dad to tell me
to make sure you went in. Now, go on.


00:43:48.920 --> 00:43:50.399
I look like a prick.


00:44:09.600 --> 00:44:10.919
Well, that went well, then.


00:44:12.720 --> 00:44:14.153
Come on.


00:44:20.480 --> 00:44:21.913
- Did you?
- Don't shout at me!


00:44:22.040 --> 00:44:23.393
I'm not shouting. Who's shouting?


00:44:24.920 --> 00:44:26.797
Did you or did you not
try and sell my typewriter?


00:44:26.920 --> 00:44:28.672
- How would you know?
- 'Cause it says in here,


00:44:28.800 --> 00:44:31.633
"For sale, Ian Dury's
fucking typewriter"!


00:44:31.760 --> 00:44:32.875
All right, I did it.


00:44:33.000 --> 00:44:34.399
- I admit it, all right?
- Hello?


00:44:35.600 --> 00:44:36.999
Ian, we need to work.


00:44:37.480 --> 00:44:39.471
But you know what, Ian?
No one fucking wanted it.


00:44:40.640 --> 00:44:43.552
I am not your fucking pet, all right?


00:44:43.920 --> 00:44:45.273
I'm as hungry for this as you are.


00:44:45.400 --> 00:44:48.437
Oh, boo. The green-eyed
monster's coming out, is it?


00:44:48.680 --> 00:44:50.750
The world doesn't revolve
around you!


00:44:50.880 --> 00:44:53.838
Oh, I think you'll find
it fucking does.


00:44:53.960 --> 00:44:57.157
- How was school?
- Okay.


00:44:58.400 --> 00:44:59.913
- Fuck you!
- Feeling left out, are you?


00:45:00.600 --> 00:45:03.512
- Double fuck you.
- Oh, fucking hell, that hurt.


00:45:03.640 --> 00:45:06.916
Write some lines!
I will show more respect!


00:45:07.040 --> 00:45:09.429
And I'm doing all this fucking work,
all this work


00:45:09.600 --> 00:45:10.999
for the family, right?


00:45:11.120 --> 00:45:13.554
You and me. You and me, it's for us.


00:45:16.400 --> 00:45:17.549
Oh, God.


00:45:17.680 --> 00:45:19.079
You fight like a bloke, Denny.


00:45:23.600 --> 00:45:25.955
Oh, great. Broke me new leg.


00:45:27.840 --> 00:45:29.353
Can you help me take it off, please?


00:45:30.040 --> 00:45:31.996
Ian? Hello?


00:45:34.200 --> 00:45:35.872
Everything you do is
for the family, is it, Ian?


00:45:36.000 --> 00:45:38.719
- Yeah, yeah.
- Right, that's fucking bollocks.


00:45:38.920 --> 00:45:41.639
Everything you do is for you,
on your terms.


00:45:41.840 --> 00:45:43.910
And if the rest of us happen
to fit along,


00:45:44.040 --> 00:45:47.316
- then that is a fucking bonus.
- Is that what you think, is it?


00:45:47.440 --> 00:45:49.590
- Yeah, that's what I think.
- Yeah? Is that what you really think?


00:45:51.240 --> 00:45:52.639
'Cause if that's right,


00:45:52.760 --> 00:45:54.990
well, you better fuck off, then,
because do you know what?


00:45:55.120 --> 00:45:56.235
I can't handle this.
I can't handle this.


00:45:56.360 --> 00:45:59.432
I'm on a flow at the moment, right?
I'm right in it. I'm right inside it.


00:45:59.560 --> 00:46:00.913
And you're getting
right inside my brain,


00:46:01.040 --> 00:46:02.871
when I'm on one,
and I won't have it, all right?


00:46:03.040 --> 00:46:04.632
So if you can't handle it,
then fuck off.


00:46:07.400 --> 00:46:09.038
You think you can do without me,
do you, Ian?


00:46:09.240 --> 00:46:11.390
- Yeah.
- Really?


00:46:14.760 --> 00:46:17.718
Oi. Can I have me leg back?


00:46:18.680 --> 00:46:21.558
Oi, don't leave me on the floor.
I'm a raspberry.


00:46:26.600 --> 00:46:27.919
Nice throw.


00:46:31.640 --> 00:46:33.039
Just easy.


00:46:33.600 --> 00:46:35.033
Got it!


00:46:36.880 --> 00:46:38.359
Fuck! Fuck!


00:46:40.120 --> 00:46:41.838
We can rebuild him.


00:46:47.960 --> 00:46:49.439
He just needs a bit of distance.


00:46:50.240 --> 00:46:52.674
I'm either too close
or not far enough away.


00:46:54.400 --> 00:46:56.231
Denise, what...


00:46:57.880 --> 00:46:59.916
What happened to him
happened a long time ago.


00:47:00.280 --> 00:47:02.032
There's nothing we can do
about it now.


00:47:04.480 --> 00:47:06.471
Everyone has their weakness.


00:47:07.920 --> 00:47:11.117
It's just that his weakness
is so obvious


00:47:11.240 --> 00:47:12.798
he doesn't need to worry about it.


00:47:14.080 --> 00:47:15.593
But what about me?


00:47:16.880 --> 00:47:18.871
What am I supposed to do?


00:47:19.720 --> 00:47:21.472
My weakness is loving him.


00:47:31.760 --> 00:47:33.034
Dad's home.


00:47:37.400 --> 00:47:38.992
I'm knocking 40.


00:47:40.120 --> 00:47:42.509
I'm a bit of a shorty.


00:47:43.600 --> 00:47:46.194
Little bit haughty,
a bit nutty, a bit naughty...


00:47:46.320 --> 00:47:48.276
Enough with the rhyming couplets.


00:47:48.400 --> 00:47:50.356
Look, I will pay front money
for the room,


00:47:50.480 --> 00:47:53.677
proper wedge.
You can be the stern landlady,


00:47:53.800 --> 00:47:55.791
with the surgical stockings
and the twinkle in her eye...


00:47:55.920 --> 00:47:57.638
- This is serious.
- I will be


00:47:57.760 --> 00:47:59.910
generally a domestic god
for the duration.


00:48:00.040 --> 00:48:01.871
I promise. Please.


00:48:02.400 --> 00:48:03.913
Oh, come on, Bet, just this once.


00:48:04.040 --> 00:48:05.632
I've got work.


00:48:11.240 --> 00:48:12.195
All right?


00:48:16.400 --> 00:48:19.039
Faster. Cured.


00:48:20.000 --> 00:48:21.831
<i>Healthy.</i>


00:48:24.400 --> 00:48:26.118
Up, up, up!


00:48:26.760 --> 00:48:29.672
Sliders out first, then walkers.
All hands on!


00:48:30.440 --> 00:48:33.193
Come on! Come on,
let's be having you.


00:48:34.000 --> 00:48:35.319
Oi, get a move on.


00:48:38.520 --> 00:48:40.033
Up, up, up!


00:48:42.040 --> 00:48:43.359
Oi, Dury, get on with it.


00:48:56.480 --> 00:48:57.799
Shitter!


00:48:58.000 --> 00:49:00.639
Shitter, shitter, shitter!


00:49:01.640 --> 00:49:03.358
- Faster. Cured.
- <i>Shitter, shitter.</i>


00:49:03.840 --> 00:49:05.512
Shitter, shitter.


00:49:06.080 --> 00:49:08.071
- Faster.
- <i>Shitter, shitter.</i>


00:49:08.200 --> 00:49:09.679
<i>- Cured.</i>
- Shitter, shitter.


00:49:10.000 --> 00:49:11.797
- Shitter, shitter.
- All right, all right!


00:49:11.960 --> 00:49:13.393
Get a move on!


00:49:18.360 --> 00:49:19.793
Where's your daddy now?


00:49:27.120 --> 00:49:30.510
Healthier. Improving.


00:49:30.720 --> 00:49:32.711
Greenness, cured.


00:49:33.520 --> 00:49:36.193
Frustration, stagger.


00:49:36.640 --> 00:49:37.959
Stun!


00:49:39.560 --> 00:49:41.676
Knock one down


00:49:42.480 --> 00:49:45.074
with a feather, clever...


00:49:45.280 --> 00:49:46.838
Clever Trevor.


00:49:47.560 --> 00:49:49.232
<i>See, the English language</i>


00:49:49.360 --> 00:49:53.319
<i>is a gloriously sophisticated</i>
<i>smorgasbord of words and phrases.</i>


00:49:53.800 --> 00:49:55.677
Songwriting's really not
that complicated.


00:49:56.120 --> 00:49:59.430
It's all about the verbals.
I'll go first.


00:50:00.360 --> 00:50:01.839
Cock.


00:50:02.160 --> 00:50:03.513
Your turn.


00:50:03.840 --> 00:50:05.193
- Willy.
- Dick.


00:50:05.440 --> 00:50:07.476
- Knob.
- Love truncheon.


00:50:07.600 --> 00:50:09.158
- Dong.
- Meat and two veg.


00:50:10.040 --> 00:50:11.359
Um...


00:50:11.480 --> 00:50:14.199
Come on,
keep them coming.


00:50:14.600 --> 00:50:16.272
- Rhythm stick.
- Chopper.


00:50:16.680 --> 00:50:18.238
- Old man.
- Pork sword.


00:50:18.880 --> 00:50:20.472
One-eyed trouser snake.


00:50:20.600 --> 00:50:21.919
Ah!


00:50:22.120 --> 00:50:24.588
Look at you all, look.
Bloody marvellous.


00:50:24.760 --> 00:50:27.593
I love being
in the warm bosoms of my family.


00:50:28.320 --> 00:50:29.673
You know why?


00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:32.958
Because I love warm bosoms.


00:50:33.440 --> 00:50:34.793
Dad...


00:50:35.160 --> 00:50:36.832
Come on, dinner's on the table.


00:51:44.240 --> 00:51:47.277
Come on, then. Touch me again
and I'll punch your head in.


00:51:48.000 --> 00:51:50.070
Kick your head in. Kick your head in!


00:51:50.520 --> 00:51:52.875
Touch me again
and I'll kick your fucking teeth


00:51:53.160 --> 00:51:54.832
so far down your Gregory Peck,


00:51:54.960 --> 00:51:56.598
you'll be able to eat
out of your Khyber Pass!


00:51:56.720 --> 00:51:58.517
- Fuck me, look who it is.
- Fuck off!


00:51:58.640 --> 00:52:00.676
Dreary Dury, the Dancing Durex.


00:52:00.800 --> 00:52:03.030
- Don't get snotty on me, posh boy.
- Leave me alone.


00:52:03.480 --> 00:52:04.799
Yeah, walk away! Fuck off!


00:52:04.920 --> 00:52:06.672
Gonna get your Spazzy Joe dad
to come and save you?


00:52:06.800 --> 00:52:08.552
'Cause guess what?
We don't give a shit who he is.


00:52:08.680 --> 00:52:10.113
- Fucking spaz.
- What's his name again?


00:52:10.240 --> 00:52:12.310
- Captain Cripple the Raspberry Ripple!
- Fuck off.


00:52:12.440 --> 00:52:13.759
Who the fuck do you think you are?


00:52:13.920 --> 00:52:16.195
You learnt some words, have you?
Proper little villain.


00:52:21.640 --> 00:52:24.871
- All right, Bax?
- All right, Strang?


00:52:25.320 --> 00:52:27.390
You know you've got blood
coming out of your nose?


00:52:35.720 --> 00:52:38.393
<i>"Who awoke the sleeping tiger?</i>


00:52:39.720 --> 00:52:41.153
"It was thee.


00:52:42.760 --> 00:52:46.594
"The dormant devil did no harm,


00:52:48.560 --> 00:52:50.073
"except to me.


00:52:52.400 --> 00:52:56.871
"The writer sat, scratching his arse,


00:52:58.120 --> 00:53:01.078
"wishing he wasn't middle class..."


00:53:18.200 --> 00:53:20.031
I've met someone else.


00:53:20.520 --> 00:53:23.034
What, around here?
You wanna be careful.


00:53:25.480 --> 00:53:28.438
He's Welsh. He does ceramics.


00:53:28.560 --> 00:53:29.959
Oh, pottery sheep?


00:53:32.720 --> 00:53:34.073
We should think about
getting a divorce.


00:53:34.200 --> 00:53:36.714
No. No.


00:53:38.480 --> 00:53:41.552
It would be better for you,
better for the kids, better for Denise.


00:53:41.680 --> 00:53:43.159
That's far too logical.


00:53:45.600 --> 00:53:49.115
No, Bet, that would be
just like tossing everything away.


00:53:50.080 --> 00:53:52.275
- Don't do this, Ian.
- I love you.


00:53:52.520 --> 00:53:54.033
I know you love me.


00:53:56.960 --> 00:53:58.552
But you don't need me.


00:54:03.560 --> 00:54:05.312
<i>There's someone else who needs me.</i>


00:54:31.480 --> 00:54:34.278
Hello. Welcome home.


00:54:35.400 --> 00:54:38.233
- I missed you.
- Oh, I missed you, too.


00:54:55.320 --> 00:54:57.993
You have painted.


00:54:58.120 --> 00:55:00.076
Mmm-hmm. Freshen it up.


00:55:01.400 --> 00:55:03.550
I thought it was looking a bit jaded.


00:55:09.640 --> 00:55:12.757
- You don't like it, do you?
- I didn't say that.


00:55:14.240 --> 00:55:15.559
But you don't.


00:55:23.040 --> 00:55:24.837
It's all very...


00:55:26.960 --> 00:55:28.279
